# OneClickTravel — the in-engine verification, replayable.
#
# What it proves, hands-free: ONE click on a discovered world-map marker fast-travels
# instantly, with no "Fast travel to X? Yes / No / Place Marker" box in between. The last
# gate IS the assertion — if the click did not travel, the replay fails there, loudly.
#
#   SKYTEST_NO_AUTOLOAD=1 skytest replay mods/OneClickTravel/build/OneClickTravel.dll \
#       oneclick.steps --headless
#
# NO_AUTOLOAD because the bundled po3_StartOnSave is stale for game 1.7.104, so boot-into-save
# is unavailable and the script drives the main menu itself. Drop that env var once Start On
# Save 2.8.0 lands in skytest/base-skse/ AND delete the first three steps.
#
# The control half of the A/B (must show the vanilla confirm box at the final click):
#   SKYTEST_NO_AUTOLOAD=1 skytest test --vanilla --headless    # then drive these steps by hand
#
# Pixel coordinates are for the headless default 1280x720; re-read them off a `shot` if the
# session resolution changes.

# --- boot: main menu -> the SkytestBase save (QASmoke) ------------------------------
click 1177 496          # CONTINUE — a coordinate click; a bare `enter` here is unreliable (#25)
wait 2s
tap enter               # "Continue from your last saved game?" -> Yes
wait until:inworld
wait 3s                 # inworld fires before the player's 3D settles (#16)

# --- stage: every marker discovered, and get OUTDOORS -------------------------------
# The console: its command table runs, unlike the probe's programmatic exec (#18).
# NOTE: `type` takes the rest of the line VERBATIM (like exec/cmd) — a trailing `# comment`
# would be typed into the console, so these comments live on their own lines.
tap tilde
wait until:menu:Console
# tmm 1 -> "All map markers shown." (shown AND fast-travelable)
type tmm 1
tap enter
wait 500ms
type coc riverwood
tap enter
wait until:cell:Riverwood
# The cell load CLOSES the console by itself — do NOT tap tilde here, that would REOPEN it, and
# an open console eats the keys below while turning the click into a console ref-pick (#27).
# This gate asserts that rather than trusting it.
wait until:!menu:Console
wait 1s
# "Enable Survival Mode?" -> No. AE offers it on the first exterior load of a save, and Survival
# Mode DISABLES fast travel. Harmless if the box is absent (an in-world click swings a fist).
click 679 548
wait 1s

# --- the test itself ----------------------------------------------------------------
tap m
wait until:menu:MapMenu
move 768 434            # hover "North Skybound Watch" (the map opens centred on Riverwood)
wait 1s
shot /tmp/oneclick-hover.png
click                   # ONE click, on the marker under the pointer
wait until:cell:NorthSkyboundWatchExterior01    # THE ASSERTION: the click alone travelled
shot /tmp/oneclick-arrived.png
